{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>In booths you shall dwell seven days</b> — corresponding to the seven clouds of glory, and corresponding to the seven days that Israel dwell in booths, they merit seven canopies, and these are they: cloud, smoke, radiance, fire, flame, the glory of the Shechinah, and the booth of Leviathan. And He commanded to make booths at the beginning of winter, for if they made them in summer it would not be discernible, but it would appear that one makes it for shade:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:22.848011873Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}